!c38'kgdevelop'!c00 is the GUI designer using Kulina graphics
library !c38'kglib'!c00. The widgets are seven different types
and  be identified  by 'widget name'. 'kgGetNamedWidget'
be  used to get a specific widget for different actions.
While other routines can change the attributes of a WIDGET,
in most cases it will be reflected only after 'kgUpdateWidget'
and a  further 'kgUpdateOn'. There is an exception in case of
'kgWrite' which is used write on 'Message Widgets'.
The available widgets can be grouped as the following seven
categories.

1. Text based input widgets.

   a. DIT (TextBox) with internal code 't'.

      DIT is a two dimensional array input boxes, where each
      boxes can have a prompt string (which can be null also).
      The input boxes can of integer, double or string type.
      There are two drawing types for 'Text Box'. Also there
      is an option to switch off 'echo'. Certainly a single
      item 'text box' is allowed.

   b. DIT  (TableBox) with code 'T', a table widget.

      This is multi-column rows of text boxes, with option
      to specify a column as 'OUTPUT' only.

   There are support routines,like 'kgGetInt' 'kgGetDouble'
   and 'kgGetString' to get values of the text boxes,
   which are numbered one dimensional arranged column wise
   starting from 1.
   Similarly there are 'kgSet...' routines also to set 
   corresponding values.
   
   DIT widgets got callbacks are called on any input action.
   However in the case of DIT with code 't', the callback
   is called only if an 'ENTER' key is pressed. This is as
   such not a problem, as other routines can access 'DIT'
   using 'kgSet..' and 'kgGet..'.

   Table related helpers.

   int kgSetOffTableCell(void *Tmp,int cell);
   int kgSetOnTableCell(void *Tmp,int cell);
   int kgGetTableColumn(void *Tmp);
   int kgGetTableRow(void *Tmp);
   int kgGetTableCell(void *Tmp);
   int kgSetTableCursor(void * Tmp,int cell);
   int kgSetTableCursorPos ( void * Tmp , int cell,int pos);
   int kgGetTableCurpos ( void *Tmp );
   int kgGetTableStartChar ( void *Tmp );
   int kgScrollDownTable(void *Tmp,int row) ;
   int kgScrollUpTable(void *Tmp,int row) ;

2. Button Types
   
   a. DIN (Buttons)
      A 2-D array of buttons.  Eleven drawing styles are available.

   b. DIL (Spl.Buttons)
      Very much similar to DIN, only difference is that, if the
      callback returns '1', then GUI will be closed. So at least
      one such button is expected in GUI, to close it.
      However any routine use kgSetExit(..) to close the GUI.

      int kgChangeButtonColor(void *Widget,int butno,int red,
                                  int green,int blue) ;
      void  kgChangeButtonTitle(void *Widget,int butno,char *title);
      char *  kgGetButtonTitle(void *Widget,int butno);
      void * kgChangeButtonNormalImage(void *Widget,int butno,void *img) ;
      void * kgChangeButtonPressedImage(void *Widget,int butno,void *img) ;

     
    
3. Slides based input WIDGETS.

   a. DID (Slidebar(I))
      DID is an integer slide with left and right arrows
      at both ends. The following routines can be used to 
      access 'DID'.

      int kgGetDslideValue(void *tmp);
      int kgSetDslideValue(void *tmp,int val);
   
   b. DIF  (Slidebar(F)))
      DIF is very much similar to DID except that it is
      used for float values. 

      float kgGetFslideValue(void *tmp);
      float kgSetFslideValue(void *tmp,float val);

   c. DIHB (Horizontal slide)
      DIHB  is also similar to DID, but without any
      arrow buttons or value display.

      int kgGetSlideValue(void *tmp);
      int kgSetSlideValue(void *tmp,int val);

4.  Browser based WIDGETS

   a. DIW  (Pulldown Browser)
      DIW  uses a 'NULL' terminated
      array of strings as its list. Helper routines be used
      set and get 'selected item' or 'selected string'.

   b. DIE  (Scroll Menu)
      A browser which uses strings as its items.
      Items are always displayed and if the portion visible
      is less than total items a vertical stroller will
      come up. It is particularly useful for bringing a menu
      list when a top bar button is pressed. The convenience
      routines , kgMenu (..), and KgMenu1(...) are useful
      for such purpose.

   c. DIRA (Radio Buttons)
      DIRA widget and the following three browser widgets use
      THUMBNAILS as its items. All the four browsers can be
      a two dimensional array of items. In case the portion 
      visible is less than the total items a vertical bar will
      appear for scrolling purpose. A THUMBNAIL got a name, 
      image and a switch. In DIRA case only one switch will be on.
      Hence it can be used to set one of the many options. 
     
   d. DICH (Check Box)
      Many switches can be made on.

   e. DIX (Selection Menu) 
      in a Spence similar to DIE but uses THUMBNAILS.
      Optionally it can be set to switch on many switches.

   f. DIY (ThumbnailBrowser)
      It is presented differently from DIX as the name of items
      are written below the image. There are drag and drop is 
      available for DIY.


   Following six Helper routines are available for all the browsers,if
   they are meaning full as per the options settings.

   char   *kgGetSelectedString(void *Tmp);
   int    kgGetSelection(void *tmp);
   int    kgSetSelection(void *tmp,int val);
   void **kgSetList(void *Widget,void **list);
   char **kgAllocStrings(char **menu);
   void **kgGetList(void *Widget);
   
   Following Helper routines are available for THUMBNAIL
   based browsers.

   int    kgSetSwitch(void *Widget,int item, int val);
   int    kgGetSwitch(void *Widget,int item);
   int    kgAddThumbNail(void *Widget,void *th,int pos);
   int    kgDeleteThumbNail(void *Widget,int pos);
   void *    kgPickThumbNail(void *Widget,int pos);
   int    kgInsertThumbNail(void *Widget,void *th,int pos);
   int kgMoveThumbNail(void *wid,int item,int pos);
   int    kgSortList(void *Widget);
   void **kgCopyList(void *Widget);
   int kgListRemoveDup(void *Wid);
   void *kgCopyThumbNail(void *th);

   Always keep in mind about the importance of 'kgUpdateWidget'
   and kgUpdateOn.

5. Scrolls INPUT WIDGET
   
   a. DIV (Vert.Scroll)
   b. DIZ (Horiz.Scroll)

    void kgSetScrollLength(void *widget,double percent);
    void kgSetScrollPos(void *widget,double percent);
    int kgSetScrollMovement ( void *Tmp , double mvnt) ;
    double  kgGetScrollPos(void *widget);
    double  kgGetScrollLength(void *widget);

6. OUTPUT only WIDGETS
   
   a. DIM with come 'm' (Message)
      Displays a single line widget
      kgWrite(..) can be used.
   
   b. DIM with code 'B' (Message(B))
      Similar to DIM (m), but look is different
      kgWrite(..) can be used.

   c. DIM with code 'M' (Display Box)
      Similar  but a different presentation
      kgWrite(..) can be used.

   d. DII (Info box) 
      Multi-line message box, but no scrolling.
      kgWrite(..) can be used.

   e. DIS (MsgScroll)
      Multi-line message box with scrolling.
      kgWrite(..) can be used.

   f. DIP (Imagebox)
      Image box to display an image
      Following routines are useful.

      void * kgSetWidgetImage(void *Widget,void *img);
      void * kgGetWidgetImage(void *Widget);

   g. DIO (ProgressBar)
      A progress bar, many types are there.
    
      void   kgSetProgressBar(void *Widget,int val);

7. DIG (Drawing area)
   
   DIG is area for drawing actions using Kulina Graphics Library.
